 following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nRio Grande Near Del Norte affecting Rio Grande County.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande River...including Del Norte...Minor flooding\nis forecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande near Del Norte.\n\n* WHEN...Until Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 7.5 feet, Major Flood. Water reaches base of Twin\nMountain Bridge on Hanna Lane Road west of Del Norte. At 6.5 feet,\nwater begins flowing over Hanna Lane Road west of Del Norte. Homes\nnear First Street and the Oak Street Bridge on Colorado Highway 112\nare threatened by high water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:45 PM MST Monday the stage was 5.8 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 5.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:45 PM MST Monday was 6.6 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall below flood stage just\nafter midnight tonight and continue falling to 3.4 feet Saturday\nafternoon.\n- Flood stage is 5.5 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-03T20:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6464bc0887f8877bfebebb5f7c89a143087a5c77.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6464bc0887f8877bfebebb5f7c89a143087a5c77.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-03T04:40:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 030440 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 940 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Strong north winds and showers/isolated t-storms on the plains into this evening, perhaps some snow showers along the Palmer Divide overnight. - Generally dry and breezy on Tue, strongest winds early in the day on the plains. - Weak trough will bring scattered show","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T08:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 020809 HWOPUB Hazardou